ilities and federal employees from providing abortion services, affecting facilities that currently receive federal funds."},{"industry":"ideological-single-issue","confidence":0.75,"rationale":"Organizations focused on reproductive health policy and abortion access or restrictions have a direct stake in the regulatory framework this bill establishes."}],"plainSummary":"This bill would make permanent the restrictions on federal funding for abortion services and health insurance coverage that includes abortion. Currently, these restrictions are renewed each year through appropriations bills; the bill would apply them across all federal programs and funds. It would also prohibit qualified health plans offered through insurance marketplaces from covering abortion. The bill includes exceptions for cases of rape, incest, or when the pregnant person's life is in danger.","classificationMethod":"llm","plain":{"whoItTouches":"Anyone who buys health insurance. Anyone who pays a medical bill.","confidence":"crs-summary"},"topOverlap":{"bioguideId":"B001260","score":0.061260165720508956},"overlapCount":107},"meaning":{"percentile":78.61317327436423,"median":0.010636331736930488,"n":6331,"ordinary":[],"unattributedShare":0.528569666281884}},{"billId":"119-hjres-88","bioguideId":"F000480","cycle":2026,"score":0.020475118112739894,"matches":[{"industry":"energy-fossil","donorAmount":63000,"donorShare":0.04303980113808301,"billConfidence":0.7,"contribution":0.010388917516089002},{"industry":"utilities-electric","donorAmount":47500,"donorShare":0.03245064371522132,"billConfidence":0.6,"contribution":0.006713926285907859},{"industry":"energy-renewable","donorAmount":20561.53,"donorShare":0.014047050195154412,"billConfidence":0.65,"contribution":0.003148476767879437},{"industry":"manufacturing","donorAmount":1000,"donorShare":0.0006831714466362383,"billConfidence":0.95,"contribution":0.0002237975428635953}],"method":{"formula":"score = Σ_industries ( donorShare(industry) × billWeight(industry) ), where billWeight = classifierConfidence / Σ classifierConfidence. Range 0–1, read as a weighted share of disclosed itemized money.","donorProfileCycle":2026,"billClassificationMethod":"llm","unclassifiedDonorShare":0.528569666281884},"bill":{"id":"119-hjres-88","congress":119,"billType":"hjres","billNumber":"88","title":"Providing congressional disapproval under chapter 8 of title 5, United States Code, of the rule submitted by the Environmental Protection Agency relating to \"California State Motor Vehicle and Engine Pollution Control Standards; Advanced Clean Cars II; Waiver of Preemption; Notice of Decision\".","introducedDate":"2025-04-02","latestActionDate":"2025-06-12","latestActionText":"Became Public Law No: 119-16.","policyArea":"Environmental Protection","subjects":["Administrative law and regulatory procedures","Air quality","California","Climate change and greenhouse gases","Congressional oversight","Environmental Protection Agency (EPA)","Federal preemption","Hybrid, electric, and advanced technology vehicles","Motor vehicles"],"sponsorBioguideId":"J000302","cosponsorCount":41,"committeeNames":[],"congressDotGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-joint-resolution/88","industries":[{"industry":"manufacturing","confidence":0.95,"rationale":"Automotive manufacturers face different emission and zero-emission vehicle requirements depending on whether California's waiver stands or is revoked."},{"industry":"energy-fossil","confidence":0.7,"rationale":"Zero-emission vehicle mandates directly affect demand for gasoline and diesel fuel in California's large vehicle market."},{"industry":"energy-renewable","confidence":0.65,"rationale":"Electric vehicle adoption rates influence demand for charging infrastructure and electricity from renewable sources."},{"industry":"utilities-electric","confidence":0.6,"rationale":"The pace of electric vehicle deployment affects electricity demand and grid infrastructure investment needs."}],"pl